      "snippet": {
        "text": "This review identified various challenges in formative assessment implementation and proposes the following strategies to improve its effectiveness: (1) Strengthen teacher training and professional development: Continuous training and support for teachers in formative assessment are critical.This includes developing their abilities to design effective assessment tools, provide constructive feedback and use assessment results to inform teaching.(2) Promote student understanding of and engagement with assessment: Educators should encourage students to participate in the assessment process, for example, through self-assessment and peer assessment.In addition, helping students understand the purpose and value of assessment can increase their acceptance of feedback and motivation.(3) Use technology to enhance assessment methods: Technology, such as online assessment tools and learning management systems, can make the assessment process more efficient, flexible and engaging.The use of technology can also enable the provision of more diverse feedback and facilitate data analysis.(4) Adjust education policies and institutions: Creating a supportive educational environment for formative assessment is essential.\n\nThis may involve adjusting curriculum standards, reducing the emphasis on standardised testing and providing more resources and time to support assessment implementation.",
