n the high school level. Bloom, et al. (1956) in his Taxonomy of Educational Objectives said that students proceed from a lower level of learning such as remembering concepts, comprehension and application to a much higher level. Mastery of the lower level should be achieved first before they are able to analyze and evaluate concepts, processes and procedures. \n\nThe five skills of English as a discipline such as reading, listening, speaking, writing and viewing need to be amplified.",
