onomous motivation and the students' perceptions of teachers' providing feedback that facilitates the monitoring of their learning progress and an understanding of how goals and criteria can be met (formative feedback). However, in the context of portfolio use, Baas et al. (2019) found an association between autonomous motivation and students' perceptions that scaffolding is integrated in their classroom practice, but not between autonomous motivation and the monitoring of growth.",
