        "text": "Consensus is growing among practitioners, scientists, and policy makers that social and emotional learning (SEL) among students is essential for their success in school and life (Halvorsen, 2024;Domitrovich et al., 2017;Domitrovich et al., 2019;Jones et al., 2017;Weissberg et al., 2015). For students to learn the SEL skills necessary, teachers must be confident in teaching these skills (Weissberg et al.,205). \n\nIn SEL intervention research, high-quality pre-intervention training for teachers (PTT) is a solid way of providing study is underlined by the need for further research on the importance of facilitators' fidelity to planned PTT, for teachers to be able to implement a SEL intervention with high quality in their own classrooms. Consequently, this study may provide knowledge essential for improvement efforts and teaching development significant to school and district leaders in the field. \n\nFacilitators' high fidelity to the planned intervention and its standardized material is necessary to achieve high-quality teacher training with adaptations that do not weaken the core elements. The quality of delivery refers to how well an intervention is delivered to achieve its intended goal and how prepared teachers are to deliver the intervention successfully in their own classrooms (Molina et al., 2022). In implementation, a support system is operationalized as strategies and practices used to support high-quality implementation (Humphrey et al., 2016). Domitrovich and colleagues (2008) introduce a multilevel conceptual framework with three interdependent levels, macro-level, school-level and individual-level, all affecting the ecological context of the implementation process and thus the quality with which the intervention is implemented and student outcomes. Hereunder, the authors focus on two levels of implementation quality, the implementation quality of the intervention itself and the support system of the intervention (Domitrovich et al., 2008). The current study focuses on the aspects of core elements, delivery, and standardization as components in the support system of the intervention for reaching implementation quality (Domitrovich et al., 2008). This study addresses the quality of implementation of the PTT in the SEL intervention curriculum ROBUST in the Resilient randomized controlled trial (RCT).",
