ment would be significantly higher than those of their peers taught by a teacher only applied formative assessment (d = 0.13, p < 0.001). When formative assessment was directed by the student, the effect size on reading achievement was larger than formative assessment with teachers' differentiated instruction, albeit not significantly (d = 0.17, p = 0.124). \n\nApart from the three pairs of contrast, the rest of the moderator variables comparisons were non-significant, although some showed significant results in subgroup analysis.",
